# CODEOWNERS — paths where a change requires Jon's review before merge.
#
# IMPORTANT: there is NO catch-all `*` owner, intentionally. The auto-merge
# workflow (.github/workflows/auto-merge.yml) relies on CODEOWNERS being
# a narrow "sensitive paths" list, not a repo-wide claim. A `*` owner would
# force Jon's review on every PR once branch protection enables "Require
# review from Code Owners", which defeats the whole triple-gate auto-merge
# design for trivial rollback-safe PRs.
#
# To enforce this file, the repo's branch protection ruleset for `main` and
# `v3/main` must have "Require review from Code Owners" enabled. Without
# that setting the file is advisory only. The auto-label workflow
# (.github/workflows/auto-label-codeowners.yml) also applies
# `needs-jon-approval` on any PR whose diff touches these paths — that
# label is the hard stop for the auto-merge workflow regardless of
# branch-protection enforcement.
#
# When editing this file, also update auto-label-codeowners.yml's regex
# (patterns inlined there because GitHub Actions has no CODEOWNERS parser).
#
# Pattern rules: last-match-wins per file.
#
# ─── 2026-11-05 T1+T2 trim ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Reduced from ~40 patterns to the 8 below. Previous breadth was imported from
# a multi-tenant SaaS context (MyZone brief) and inappropriate for a solo
# lifestyle-business repo. Subagent writes to removed surfaces are now
# guarded by `.claude/settings.json` deny rules instead.
# See claude/merge-autonomy-recommendations.md §3 and
# claude/session-7-handover.md §4 for the rationale.
#
# THE 14 PATTERNS (keep this list in sync with the entries below AND with the
# regex in .github/workflows/auto-label-codeowners.yml and auto-merge.yml's
# CO_RE — a pattern missing from that regex is a GAP; a regex alternation
# missing from here is a LEAK; scripts/check_codeowners_drift.py fails CI on
# either):
#
#   1  apps/web/src/lib/billing/**
#   2  apps/worker/src/worker/billing/**
#   3  apps/web/src/app/api/billing/**
#   4  apps/web/src/app/api/entitlements/**
#   5  apps/worker/migrations/*_v3_commercial*.sql
#   6  .github/workflows/**
#   7  .github/CODEOWNERS
#   8  AGENTS.md
#   9  CLAUDE.md          (any depth)        — added 2026-11-22, §11 R5
#  10  **/.claude/**      (any depth)        — added 2026-11-22, §11 R5
#  11  **/SKILL.md        (any depth)        — added 2026-11-22, §11 R5
#  12  CLAUDE.local.md    (any depth)        — added 2026-11-22, §11 R5 review
#  13  .mcp.json          (any depth)        — added 2026-11-22, §11 R5 review
#  14  scripts/**                            — added 2026-11-22, §11 R5
#
# The count is enumerated rather than stated because a bare number goes stale
# silently (this header once said "6" when the real count was 8). Agreement
# with the regex copies is no longer an audit claim here: it is enforced on
# every PR by scripts/check_codeowners_drift.py, run in the required Lint job.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Stripe / billing lib paths — money surface, requires Jon on every edit.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
apps/web/src/lib/billing/**                     @JDC000000
apps/worker/src/worker/billing/**               @JDC000000
apps/web/src/app/api/billing/**                 @JDC000000
apps/web/src/app/api/entitlements/**            @JDC000000

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Commercial (Stripe-touching) database migrations only.
# Non-commercial migrations are now agent-mergeable under the standard
# triple-gate; a commercial migration is the one that lands against prod
# billing tables.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
apps/worker/migrations/*_v3_commercial*.sql     @JDC000000

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CI / workflow surfaces — infrastructure of merge-gating itself.
# Bootstrap self-protect: if auto-merge.yml or sibling workflows could be
# edited without CODEOWNER review, the entire gating system is bypassable.
# CODEOWNERS itself is listed because `.github/workflows/**` does not match
# `.github/CODEOWNERS`; without this line a PR could narrow CODEOWNERS to
# nothing and then merge anything.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.github/workflows/**                            @JDC000000
.github/CODEOWNERS                              @JDC000000

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Prompt-injection surface — the files that instruct agents.
# AGENTS.md is the single doc read by every agent session.
#
# 2026-11-22 (AGENTIC-L5-PLAN §11 R5): CLAUDE.md, .claude/** and SKILL.md
# were previously unowned on the theory that CLAUDE.md is "a thin pointer to
# AGENTS.md". That theory does not survive contact with the runtime: Claude
# Code loads CLAUDE.md (at any depth), .claude/settings.json (permission
# allow/deny), .claude/agents/*.md (subagent tool grants) and SKILL.md files
# as INSTRUCTIONS, before it reads AGENTS.md. A PR that edits them changes
# what every later agent session is allowed and told to do — the same class
# as AGENTS.md. Until this change they were also reachable by the now-retired
# fast-path arm (`*.md` anywhere), i.e. mergeable with zero review.
# The `**/` forms are deliberate: nested .claude/ directories and SKILL.md
# files are loaded too, so root-only would be a GAP.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
AGENTS.md                                       @JDC000000
CLAUDE.md                                       @JDC000000
**/.claude/**                                   @JDC000000
**/SKILL.md                                     @JDC000000
# Also loaded by Claude Code as instructions/config: personal memory file and
# MCP server definitions (which servers an agent session connects to).
CLAUDE.local.md                                 @JDC000000
.mcp.json                                       @JDC000000

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# scripts/** — the merge rail (safe_merge.sh), every CI gate (check_*.py,
# _gate_exit.py), the staging smoke gate and its sweeper. A weakened gate is
# invisible by construction (the suite goes green either way), so these are
# owned as a CLASS, not by filename. Added 2026-11-22, §11 R5; this is also
# what makes the orchestrator merge gate (R6, scripts/or4-merge.sh) owned
# once it is committed.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
scripts/**                                      @JDC000000
